   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 58 of the laws of 2013 amending the environmental\nconservation law and the state finance law relating to the \"Cleaner, Greener\nNY Act of 2013\", in relation to the effectiveness thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S6481",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6481-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd part F §12, Chap 58 of 2013",
    "lawSection": "Environmental Conservation",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S6481\n\nSPONSOR: KAPLAN\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend chapter 58 of the laws of 2013 amend-\ning the environmental conservation law and the state finance law relat-\ning to the \"Cleaner, Greener NY Act of 2013\", in relation to the effec-\ntiveness thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to extend certain local enforcement authori-\nty for the bottle bill.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis bill would authorize New York City, Nassau and Suffolk County to\nretain their authority to enforce certain bottle bill provision s for an\nadditional two years.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nIn 2013, New York City, Suffolk, and Nassau County received authori-\nzation to enforce provisions related to the sale of bottles without the\nrequired bottle deposit of five cents. In exchange for enforcement such\nmunicipalities were authorized to retain 25 percent of all resulting\nfines. The authority for this enforcement is set to expire on April 1,\n2019. This legislation would extend such authority until April 1, 2021.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2017-2018: Chapter 58 of the Laws of 2017\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
